%S A397815 1,1,3,16,168,4394,265422,33605540,8591054164,4398081646632,
%T A397815 4503601202870488,9223372136642857120,37778931871856719415312,
%U A397815 309485009822473297369710816,5070602400913121023205596769760,166153499473114535887930783082405376,10889035741470030849400125017819216953408
%N A397815 a(n) is the number of different ways to tile an n X n square lattice with corners, up to rotations and reflections.
%C A397815 A corner is the union of two perpendicular line segments of unit length.
%C A397815 Equivalently, a(n) is the number of non-isomorphic domino tilings of the order n Aztec diamond. - _Andrew Howroyd_, Aug 10 2026
%H A397815 Nicolay Avilov, <a href="/A397815/a397815.jpg">Graphic representation of the first three terms</a>.
%H A397815 Yi-Lin Lee, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2303.02750">Off-diagonally symmetric domino tilings of the Aztec diamond</a>, arXiv:2303.02750 [math.CO], 2023.
%H A397815 Wikipedia, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aztec_diamond">Aztec diamond</a>.
%H A397815 Bo-Yin Yang, <a href="https://dspace.mit.edu/handle/1721.1/13937">Two Enumeration Problems about the Aztec Diamonds</a>, MIT, 1991.
%F A397815 From _Andrew Howroyd_, Aug 10 2026: (Start)
%F A397815 a(n) ~ 2^(n*(n+1)/2-3).
%F A397815 a(n) = (A006125(n+1) + A372145(n) + 2*A374153(n) + 2*Q(n))/8 where Q(4*n-1) = A059487(n), Q(4*n) = 2^n*A059487(n), Q(4*n-2) = Q(4*n-3) = 0. (End)
%e A397815 a(1) = 1 because a 1 X 1 square can be divided into corners in only one way: by making two cuts at opposite vertices of the square.
%Y A397815 Cf. A006125, A059487, A134438, A220054, A372145, A374153.
%K A397815 nonn,new
%O A397815 0,3
%A A397815 _Nicolay Avilov_, Aug 09 2026
%E A397815 a(7) onward from _Andrew Howroyd_, Aug 10 2026
